{"title":"1980 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A gambling student tosses a fair coin. She gains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> point for each head that turns up, and gains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> points for each tail that turns up. Prove that the probability of the student scoring exactly <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> points is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/c/57c992637c8da68133e175e56ecbad1cd4f8eaf4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot\\left(2+\\left(-\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{n}\\right)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"157\" height=\"55\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Yes\nProof:\nEach row has 10 numbers.\nFor the 1rst row let's call them <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/9/e796d31078cd07745d0f9bb5bd9cf52d5619353e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2\\dots,a_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"13\" />\nFor the 2nd row let's call them <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/0/64066c898104bb7950983e37cd7c2872dc43b029.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b_1,b_2\\dots,b_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"18\" />\nFor the 3rd row let's call them <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/8/3/883652993ed0ebb992ced479b565b95481bb2a56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c_1,c_2\\dots,c_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"98\" height=\"13\" />\nFor the 4th row let's call them <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/c/fbcf9be02648886a3fcc0ce024658b49bd8c41a1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d_1,d_2\\dots,d_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"18\" />\nFor the 5th row let's call them <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/9/039cc16d2846e9754f6111f17e23bca06b4e3707.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$e_1,e_2\\dots,e_{10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"100\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p>let's consider the 7th column.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/8/a/28aa9afeea710fb8465bcdb2ea4325e4b7019f7f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$max(a_7,b_7,c_7,d_7,e_7)&gt;max(a_6,b_6,c_6,d_6,e_6)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"352\" height=\"20\" />\nWe want to prove that the 2nd largest in the 7th column\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_Canadian_MO\" title=\"1980 Canadian MO\">1980 Canadian MO</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_Canadian_MO\" title=\"1980 Canadian MO\">1980 Canadian MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_Canadian_MO_Problems\" title=\"1980 Canadian MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>Problem 3</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1980 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1980 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1980 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1980 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1980_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1980 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017173402\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.019 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 81/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 716/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 43/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1924/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.572      1 Template:CanadaMO_box\n100.00%    6.572      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:18273:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017173402 and revision id 288811. Rendering was t